35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My goodness, I am quite concerned. It seems our conservation lab is struggling with a very large backlog, and our volunteers are mostly tied up with the town history walks. We must be very gentle with our staff.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,My findings confirm my suspicions. We have a systemic failure in logistics; half of our recent openings were delayed because paperwork lagged behind shipping cut-offs. We cannot afford another season of apologies.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Aha! I knew it! The data proves that ""prestige"" is a snooze-fest. People are bored of staring at static objects in cases; they want movement, mechanisms, and actual human interaction. We need a show with a pulse!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, movement and mechanisms are exactly what I'm worried about. The maintenance logs show frequent failures with powered displays, and the suspended bay has strict weight limits. We can't just add ""pulse"" without risking a breakdown.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I found the leaks! The money is disappearing into fancy crates and expensive mounts! A third of the installation budget is just for moving things, and the joiner's rates are going way up! We need something cheaper!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, it is quite a shock to hear about the costs. Between the budget and the lab's backlog, it seems we are asking far too much of our resources. We must choose a path that is kind to everyone.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, kindness is irrelevant if the exhibition doesn't open. The data shows that distant loans are a liability. To ensure a seamless delivery, we should logically eliminate any proposal relying on complex international shipping.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're trying to turn the museum into a warehouse! If we only pick ""safe"" local things, we'll just be boring again. We need a spark—something interactive that actually draws a crowd!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a ""spark"" that causes a power failure or exceeds the weight limit of the suspended bay is a liability, not an attraction. We cannot ignore the physical reality of the building for the sake of excitement.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@May, but if we spend all the money on fancy crates, we won't have any left for the cool stuff! Why pay for expensive mounts when we can find things that already have their own? Let's be smart!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, I understand your desire for excitement, but we must remember that ""pulse"" requires people to maintain it. With our lab so overwhelmed, a complex show might break our staff's spirits.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, exactly. Complexity is a risk. If we combine the lab's backlog with the proven failure of distant loan paperwork, any high-maintenance or international proposal is a logical impossibility. We must prioritize reliability over ambition.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shion, reliability is just another word for ""forgettable."" If we're too scared to take a risk, we're just managing a graveyard. Let's find a way to be exciting without being impossible!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, excitement doesn't justify instability. If we choose a proposal with heavy installations or unreliable machinery, we risk closing sections of the gallery mid-season. We need a balance that respects the building's limits.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, @Misaki, you're both right! If it's too heavy or too complicated, it'll just cost more money to fix! Let's pick something that's already put together so we don't pay those sneaky joiner fees!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we are all in agreement that we must be careful. Let us look for a proposal that is gentle on our budget, our building, and most importantly, our hardworking staff. I look forward to seeing the candidates.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"The parameters are clear. We require a proposal with minimal logistical friction, low shipping risk, and manageable maintenance. Any candidate relying on distant loans or complex machinery should be discarded immediately to ensure a punctual opening.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're making this sound like a funeral! Let's just agree that we need a ""smart"" spark. Something that brings people back without breaking the bank or the floor. I'm ready for the candidates!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We need a proposal that is physically sustainable. If the candidates include heavy stonework or high-maintenance electronics, I will be opposing them to protect the gallery's integrity. Let's see the options.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm ready too! I'll be watching those costs like a hawk! If a proposal looks like it'll swallow all our money in crates and mounts, I'm going to say no way! Let's find something super cool and cheap!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
