60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at these, Option A seems the most gentle. Local textiles would not strain our shipping budget, and the demonstrations would bring a lovely, human warmth without overwhelming our tired staff.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, I agree. Option A is the only logical choice. It eliminates the risk of shipping delays and paperwork failures entirely. Options C and D are logistical nightmares waiting to happen, and B puts too much pressure on the lab.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're so predictable! But look at Option B—a working conservation bench! That's exactly the kind of human interaction and ""pulse"" that actually brings people back. It's way more exciting than just looking at clothes.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a working bench in the gallery sounds interesting, but Option B involves municipal digs. If that means heavy stone or soil reconstructions, we risk exceeding the suspended bay's weight limit. Option A is the safest for the building.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@May, a working bench sounds fun, but @Shizue said the lab is already super tired! We can't give them more work! Option A is local, so no scary shipping costs or expensive crates. It's the cheapest and best!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, your heart is in the right place, but a working bench in the gallery would be a heavy burden for our lone conservationist. We must protect their well-being. Option A is a much kinder choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@May, your desire for ""pulse"" is a luxury we cannot afford. Option B increases the lab's workload, and Option C's rigging is a structural risk. Option A is the only candidate that guarantees a punctual opening.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're treating this like a math problem, not a museum! Option A is safe, sure, but it's a bit sleepy. Still, if the ""pulse"" comes from the craftspeople's demonstrations, it might actually work!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, if the demonstrations are the focus, it provides the interaction you want without the structural risks of Option C or the weight concerns of Option B. It is the most sustainable choice for the gallery.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@May, see! Option A can be exciting too! Plus, since it's local, we won't waste money on those sneaky shipping crates. It's like a win-win! Let's go with the one that doesn't eat our budget!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am so glad we are finding common ground. Option A allows us to celebrate our community's talents while ensuring our staff can breathe and smile again. It truly feels like the most harmonious choice for everyone.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, harmony is a byproduct of efficiency. By removing the variables of international shipping and structural instability, we eliminate the possibility of failure. Option A is the only choice that satisfies every constraint logically.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"Fine, you've won me over! If the craftspeople bring the energy, Option A isn't just safe—it's smart. It gives the visitors that human connection they crave without breaking the bank or the floor. I'm in!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Option A avoids the weight risks of Option B and the electrical failures of Option C. It is the only proposal that ensures the gallery remains functional and safe for the entire season.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! Everyone agrees! Option A is the winner because it's local, friendly, and won't let our money vanish into thin air. No sneaky crates for us! I'm voting for Option A!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It has been a lovely discussion. I am heartened that we have found a path that respects both our visitors and our wonderful staff. I shall cast my vote for Option A.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,The conclusion is inevitable. Option A is the only proposal that eliminates logistical risk and ensures a punctual opening. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"I'll go with the flow! Since it's got that human touch with the demonstrations and won't bore the visitors to tears, it's a winner in my book. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Option A is the only choice that respects the physical limits of the building and avoids the risk of mid-season closures. It is the most responsible decision. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm so happy we all agree! Option A is the best because it's super safe for the budget and won't let the money disappear! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
